  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 135 PM CDT Fri Jul 17 2026\n\nThrough the weekend and into next week, the large scale pattern will \nbecome drier and more stable as surface and mid-level high pressure \ngradually build westward. Increasing sunshine and the drier air mass \nwill allow temperatures to gradually warm, with highs near \nseasonal normals this weekend before climbing a few degrees above \naverage early next week. Heat index values are expected to remain \ngenerally between 100-105 degF, supporting a moderate (level 2 of \n4) heat risk across much of the region. The hottest conditions are\nanticipated across the Rio Grande Plains and Brush Country, where\nsome locations could approach the triple digits with isolated \npockets of major (level 3 of 4) heat risk.",
